  "system": {
    "slug": "mystaria-stage-1",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 3
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>Mystaria is at the first stage of Cerberus augmentation — a promising operative whose natural agility and combat instincts made her a candidate for the Phantom program. Her cybernetics are minimal but effective: enhanced reflexes, hardened skeletal plating, and a prototype phase cloak implant that requires full regeneration between uses. She fights with a plasma sword and hold-out pistol, relying on ambush and precision over sustained firepower.</p><p><strong>Sneak Attack:</strong> Mystaria deals an extra 1d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p><p><strong>Phantom Cloak (1 action, 1/encounter):</strong> Mystaria activates her prototype phase cloak, becoming Invisible until the end of her next turn or until she makes a Strike.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Barrier:</strong> 30 Shield HP. Recharges 10 HP per turn.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
